---
description: Prohibit low-value comments that restate the code. Enforce comments that explain non-obvious intent.
alwaysApply: true
---

# Comment Quality

Only write a comment when the code cannot speak for itself.

## Never write comments that

- Restate what the code does (`# Increment counter`, `# Return result`, `// Import the module`)
- Narrate an assignment (`task_data = event  # Data comes from EventBridge`)
- Duplicate a function signature in prose (`# This function handles the connection`)
- Mark obvious sections (`# Variables`, `# Main logic`, `# Error handling`)
- Explain a change being made (no `# Added this for migration`, `# Now using zip instead of image`)

## Write comments only when

- The code makes a non-obvious trade-off that has a reason (e.g. why a timeout is 5s and not 30s)
- A constraint exists outside the codebase (regulatory, infra quirk, external API behavior)
- A deliberate workaround for a known bug or limitation is in place

## Examples

```python
# BAD
task_data = event  # Data comes from Input defined in EventBridge
logger.setLevel(logging.INFO)  # Set log level

# GOOD
payload_part += "=" * (4 - len(payload_part) % 4)  # base64 padding: JWT segments are unpadded
```

```hcl
# BAD
resource "aws_lambda_function" "notifications" {  # Lambda function for notifications

# GOOD
  timeout = 30  # EventBridge retries on timeout; keep above Django's median task duration (p95 ~22s)
```
